<title>INDIA: Indian cotton markets shut for religious holiday.</title>
<headline>Indian cotton markets shut for religious holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian cotton markets remained shut for the second successive day on Tuesday for the local Jain festival, dealers said. The markets reopen on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They were closed on Monday for another festival.</p>
<p>On the last trading day on Friday, higher offering by Indian state firms held cotton prices from gainingy, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
